From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:30:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] test: native async tests, shared fixtures, OpenAI
 contract test for /v1

- pytest-asyncio (`asyncio_mode = auto`, pytest.ini). A libcst codemod
  (scripts/codemods/asyncio_run_to_async_tests.py, kept for reference)
  rewrote 320 `def test(): async def run(): ...; asyncio.run(run())` tests
  into plain `async def test()` bodies and turned 336 other
  `asyncio.run(x)` calls inside tests into `await x`. Six helper-level
  `asyncio.run` remain on purpose; test_redis_client_singleton keeps two
  because it proves two *different* event loops never share a client.
- tests/conftest.py: `engine` (SQLite, or TEST_DATABASE_URL), `session_factory`,
  `db_session`, `user`, `admin`, and `client` (httpx over the real app with
  `get_db` overridden). New tests use these; the 103 existing
  `create_async_engine` helpers stay until the file they live in is touched.
- tests/test_gateway_openai_contract.py pins the /v1/chat/completions wire
  format: text/event-stream, every frame a valid `chat.completion.chunk`
  (pydantic model in the test), Alpharouter trailer last, exactly one
  `[DONE]`, 400 for stream=false, 401 without a key.
- Stream error frames are now OpenAI-shaped:
  `{"error": {"message", "type": "provider_error", "code": null}}` via
  `_sse_error_frame()` (was a bare string, which OpenAI SDKs render as
  "undefined"). ChatPanel already accepted both forms.
- requirements-dev.txt pins pytest/pytest-asyncio/ruff/mypy/mypy-baseline/
  vulture; CI installs it; pytest runs from backend/ (`pythonpath = .`).

Verified: 1372 passed / 6 skipped (SQLite), Postgres canary 11 passed,
contract test fails when the error frame is reverted to the old shape.

